<i>See</i> <i>State of Oregon, Department of Justice,</i> <i>Atty. Gen. Pub=
lic Records and Meetings Manual</i>, 19-20 (2024).<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"margin-bottom:8.0pt;line-height:105%"><b><s=
pan style=3D"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:105%;font-family:&quot;Calibri&qu=
ot;,sans-serif">Fee Waiver Request Analysis<o:p></o:p></span></b></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Ca=
libri&quot;,sans-serif">Applying the relevant factors helps us determine wh=
ether the PRR is in the public interest. The requester has demonstrated tha=
t this request relates to a personal, rather than
 a public interest. Therefore, this factor does not weigh in favor of grant=
ing a fee waiver.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Ca=
libri&quot;,sans-serif"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Ca=
libri&quot;,sans-serif">The second factor is the purpose for which the requ=
ester intends to use the information. The requester has not demonstrated th=
at this factor weighs in favor of granting a fee
 waiver as the use of records for a personal issue does not weigh in favor =
of the request being in the public interest.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Ca=
libri&quot;,sans-serif"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Ca=
libri&quot;,sans-serif">The third factor is the character of the informatio=
n. The requester has not demonstrated that this factor weighs in favor of g=
ranting a fee waiver as the fee waiver request
 form does not explain how the release of records is in the public interest=
 other than by stating a general interest in transparency.<o:p></o:p></span=
></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Ca=
libri&quot;,sans-serif"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Ca=
libri&quot;,sans-serif">The fourth factor is whether the requested informat=
ion is already in the public domain. The requester has not demonstrated tha=
t this factor weighs in favor of granting a fee
 waiver.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Ca=
libri&quot;,sans-serif"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Ca=
libri&quot;,sans-serif">The final factor is whether the requester can demon=
strate the ability to disseminate the information to the public. The reques=
ter has not demonstrated the ability to disseminate
 the public records but merely stated that he can post it on a website.<o:p=
></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Ca=
libri&quot;,sans-serif"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"margin-bottom:8.0pt;line-height:105%"><span=
 style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;line-height:105%;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;=
,sans-serif">Finally, in evaluating a public records request fee waiver the=
 public body must consider whether, under the totality
 of the circumstances, a fee waiver is also in the public interest. When we=
ighing the public interest in disclosure versus the public interest in pres=
erving public funds, when none of the prescribed factors weigh in favor of =
the grant of a fee waiver, the grant
 of a fee waiver is not warranted. Consequently, your request for a fee wai=
ver is denied.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"margin-bottom:8.0pt;line-height:105%"><b><s=
